<div class="note-content"><p> If the officer held you on suspicion of a warrant then released you when s/he found out there was not warrant, the detention may have been unlawful and actionable in the courts. This will depend on the nature of the belief the officer has. If it is shown that the officer never had credible evidence of a warrant, but merely an unsupported supposition, the detention may be actionable in the civil courts. </p></div>
