<li class="node-level-9" id="node_443" data-answer-type="yes" style="display:none;">
<div class="node-container">
<div class="node-content-stack">
<div class="node-text note-trigger" data-original-text="Yes -- Did the officer take you to the nearest magistrate?">
<span class="question-text">Yes -- Did the officer take you to the nearest magistrate?</span>
<span class="inline-buttons">
<button class="yes-button tiny" data-node-id="node_443" data-hyperlink="../ExaminingTrial/examining%20trial.html" data-child-id="node_444">Yes</button>
<button class="no-button tiny" data-node-id="node_443" data-hyperlink="" data-child-id="node_445">No</button>
</span>
</div>
<div class="note-content"><div class="fact" answer="yes"> <p> After arrest, the arresting officer is required to take you directly to the nearest magistrate. If you are arrested for an on sight offense, the officer is required by Texas Code of Criminal Procedure 14.06 to take you directly to the nearest magistrate: </p> <p> <span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 47.3426px; text-transform: none; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); display: inline !important; float: none"><font color="rgb(0, 0, 0)" face="Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="16px">Art. 14.06. MUST TAKE OFFENDER BEFORE MAGISTRATE. (a) Except as otherwise provided by this article, in each case enumerated in this Code, the person making the arrest or the person having custody of the person arrested shall take the person arrested or have him taken without unnecessary delay, but not later than 48 hours after the person is arrested, before the magistrate who may have ordered the arrest, before some magistrate of the county where the arrest was made without an order, or, to provide more expeditiously to the person arrested the warnings described by Article </font></span><a target="new" href="https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/GetStatute.aspx?Code=CR&Value=15.17" style="text-decoration: none; font-family: Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 47.3426px; text-transform: none; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)"><font face="Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="16px">15.17</font></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 47.3426px; text-transform: none; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); display: inline !important; float: none"><font color="rgb(0, 0, 0)" face="Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="16px"> of this Code, before a magistrate in any other county of this state. The magistrate shall immediately perform the duties described in Article </font></span><a target="new" href="https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/GetStatute.aspx?Code=CR&Value=15.17" style="text-decoration: none; font-family: Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 47.3426px; text-transform: none; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)"><font face="Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="16px">15.17</font></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 47.3426px; text-transform: none; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); display: inline !important; float: none"><font color="rgb(0, 0, 0)" face="Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="16px"> of this Code.</font></span> </p> <p> </p> <p> If you are arrested on a warrant, Texas Code of Criminal Procedure 15.16 requires the arresting officer to take you to the nearest magistrate as follows: </p> <p> </p> <p> <span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 47.3426px; text-transform: none; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); display: inline !important; float: none"><font color="rgb(0, 0, 0)" face="Courier New, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="16px">Art. 15.16. HOW WARRANT IS EXECUTED. (a) The officer or person executing a warrant of arrest shall without unnecessary delay take the person or have him taken before the magistrate who issued the warrant or before the magistrate named in the warrant, if the magistrate is in the same county where the person is arrested. If the issuing or named magistrate is in another county, the person arrested shall without unnecessary delay be taken before some magistrate in the county in which he was arrested.</font></span> </p> </div></div>
</div>
<div class="question-comment always-visible">
<input type="text" class="comment-textbox" placeholder="Leave comments or questions here" size="50" id="textbox-node_443">
</div>
</div>
<ul class="child-nodes" data-parent-id="node_443" style="display:none;">
<li class="node-level-10" id="node_445" data-answer-type="no" style="display:none;">
<div class="node-container">
<div class="node-content-stack">
<div class="node-text note-trigger" data-original-text="No -- To your knowledge, did the officer make a due diligent effort to locate a magistrate for the purpose of an examining trial?">
<span class="question-text">No -- To your knowledge, did the officer make a due diligent effort to locate a magistrate for the purpose of an examining trial?</span>
